  "diagnosis_conclusion": "The large recall collapse on Botnet (99.8% in-sample calibrated val -> 50.04% sealed test) and DDoS (100% in-sample val -> 53.44% sealed test) was caused by a combination of: (1) In-sample calibration optimism in Phase 12 where calibrators were fit and tested on the exact same validation partition; (2) Temporal leakage and chunk-order shift where time_of_day_cos and time_of_day_sin (ranks 3 and 4 in V2) separated early-chunk validation flows from late-chunk test flows with high adversarial AUC; (3) Over-confident default operating thresholds (P >= 0.70) without cross-fitted calibration on untouched test distributions."
